      <uighur>boqda</uighur>
      <cyrillic>богд</cyrillic>
      <transcript>BOΓDA</transcript>
      <definition>adj. and n. Holy, sacred, divine; august; a holy one.</definition>
      <page>111</page>
      <examples>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠪᠣᠬᠳᠠ ᠡᠵᠡᠨ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- ezen</transcript>
          <definition> The holy lord or master; [His or Your] Majesty.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠪᠣᠬᠳᠠ ᠬᠠᠭᠠᠨ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- xaγan, </transcript>
          <definition>The Holy Khan (a title of Mongolian khans)</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠠᠷᠤ ᠪᠣᠬᠳᠠ</unicode>
          <transcript>aru --</transcript>
          <definition>'The Northern Bogdo'  (a respectful term of reference to the Grand Lama of Urga)</definition>
        </example>
      </examples>
